/*
    On set operands, `B ^ A` denotes the set of functions from `A` to `B`. This is the
    usual reading of exponentiation on sets: the exponent is the domain and the base is
    the codomain.
    So `string ^ int` is the same set as `int ^^ string`, since `^^` is just `^` with its
    operands reversed. The two spellings differ only in which end is written first.
*/

string ^ int
